# Copy to config/shop_calculators and fill in. Gitignored, because the real one
# names the client's shops.
#
# Which of his shipping calculators each shop offers in its Calculator dropdown.
#
#   <shop>: ClassName ClassName ...
#
# Class names are resolved under Spree::Calculator::Shipping, from the files in
# app/models/spree/calculator/shipping, which is gitignored and shipped as a
# deploy asset for the same reason this file is.
#
# ── why per shop at all ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One image serves every shop, each with its own database and its own SHOP.
# Registering every calculator on every shop would offer one country's freight
# table in another country's admin, and the wrong table picked once is wrong on
# every order after it. The client's own shop shows four entries, all of them
# his and all of them for that country.
#
# ── what happens without this file ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The initializer raises. That is deliberate: the calculators are registered
# with Spree at boot, and a shop that boots without them still works. It shows
# the six calculators Spree ships with, the client's freight table is missing
# from the list, and an existing shipping method keeps quoting correctly until
# somebody edits it. Nothing fails and nothing logs.
#
# That is exactly what he photographed on 24 August: his own shop offering his
# calculator by name, the new one offering only Spree's six.
example-shop: SomeShippingCalculator FreePostageCalculator
